        // Drift catch — clause (162)'s empty-slice + flat-histogram +
        // matching-singleton fixpoint arms fire when an override folds
        // the set-level middle-band uniqueness predicate onto `true`
        // unconditionally. Empty-slice arm produces `true != false`;
        // every flat-histogram + matching-singleton arm produces
        // `true != false` at cardinality `>= 2` because on those
        // fixtures no variant falls in the strict interior.
